# Rank 1272 / CVE-2020-19825: Kimai rendered a timesheet entry's
# user-supplied description through its Markdown-to-HTML helper and echoed
# the result directly into the response. The Twig `desc2html` filter that
# wraps this call is declared `is_safe: ['html']`, so nothing downstream
# escapes the converted output, and the Markdown parser itself runs with
# HTML passthrough enabled -- a description containing raw `<script>` markup
# reaches the browser unescaped. `App\Utils\Markdown::toHtml($text, $safe)`
# passes its flag straight to Parsedown's `setSafeMode`, where `true`
# neutralizes injected markup and `false` lets it pass through, and
# `timesheetContent` -- the callable behind `desc2html` and `comment2html`
# -- spells it `toHtml($content, false)` at both revisions.
#
# The fix (kimai/kimai@a0e8aa3a43, PR #962) touches seven files: six
# `.twig` templates change `{{ entry.description|desc2html }}` to
# `{{ entry.description|escape|desc2html }}`, and
# `src/Twig/MarkdownExtension.php` flips `markdownToHtml` from
# `toHtml($content, true)` to `toHtml($content, false)`. That one PHP line
# is not a discriminator in either direction: it backs the separate `md2html`
# filter, which no template and no production PHP code calls at either
# revision (only the unit test does), and the flip moves it toward unsafe
# -- Parsedown safe mode off -- not toward the patched behaviour. The
# remediation is entirely the `|escape` at the six template call sites.
#
# VyQL has no Twig frontend at all -- every `.twig` file in a real checkout
# is skipped with "matched no frontend" -- so the actual vulnerable and
# patched lines can never be scanned, and the vulnerable PHP spelling is
# byte-identical across the two revisions, so no PHP-side discriminator
# exists either. This spec instead pins the equivalent taint shape in the
# PHP half of the same data flow (untrusted description reaching a
# non-sanitizing Markdown-to-HTML call, then an unescaped HTML sink) to show
# the existing rule judging this shape correctly in isolation; the miss is
# specific to the Twig template layer, not to the rule or binding. See the
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry for the frontend gap this rank is blocked on.

test "rank1272: timesheet description reaches markdown-to-html and is echoed raw"
  lang php
  profile web
  file TimesheetController.php
  expect VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  <?php
  class TimesheetController {
    private $markdown;

    public function renderDescription() {
      $description = $_POST['description'];
      $html = $this->markdown->toHtml($description, false);
      echo $html;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1272: timesheet description is escaped before markdown-to-html"
  lang php
  profile web
  file TimesheetController.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  <?php
  class TimesheetController {
    private $markdown;

    public function renderDescription() {
      $description = $_POST['description'];
      $escaped = htmlspecialchars($description, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8');
      $html = $this->markdown->toHtml($escaped, false);
      echo $html;
    }
  }
  ```
